  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Objective**: Replace a small link icon in the chat header with a more prominent, user-friendly indicator that shows whether parent content is connected or disconnected from the current chat.\n\n2. **Solution**: Create a new `ParentContentIndicator.vue` component that displays as a banner or badge above the message list, clearly showing parent connection status with toggle functionality.\n\n3. **Design Variants**: Three designs provided\u2014A (inline compact banner), B (card-style badge with visual prominence), and C (minimal collapsible chevron)\u2014all using Tailwind CSS and DaisyUI components.\n\n4. **Key Features**: Each variant shows parent chat name, connection status, and a toggle button; uses color coding (info=connected, warning=disconnected) for instant visual feedback.\n\n5. **Integration**: Component replaces the header button, integrates above the Chat component in ChatView.vue, and maintains existing toggle behavior while improving UX clarity and accessibility.",
